# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lead capture. Three independent channels; a lead is safe if ANY one delivers.
# Every variable here is SERVER-ONLY — never add the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix to any
# of them, or the credential ships to every visitor's browser.
# Full setup instructions: docs/lead-pipeline-setup.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. THE RECORD — Google Sheet, written through an Apps Script web app.
#    This is the surface the ops team works: call notes, status, outcome.
#    The secret is checked inside the script, so a leaked URL alone cannot
#    write rows.
SHEET_WEBHOOK_URL=
SHEET_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# 2. PRIMARY ALERT — WhatsApp Cloud API.
#    The sender number must belong to the WhatsApp Business Account and must
#    NOT also be signed in to the ordinary WhatsApp app.
#    Business-initiated messages need an approved template, so the lead details
#    travel as template parameters: {{1}} name {{2}} phone {{3}} area {{4}} ref
WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_ALERT_TO=            # who gets told, e.g. 923288489988
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NAME=new_lead
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANG=en

# 3. BACKUP ALERT — Telegram bot.
#    Point the chat id at a GROUP, not one person: whoever is on shift sees the
#    lead instead of it waiting on a single phone.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics. Completely inert while unset: no script loads, nothing collected.
# BEFORE SETTING THIS: GA4 writes cookies. NORTH-STAR ledger 28 accepts running
# without a consent banner on today's facts, and names the two triggers that
# should reopen that — ads aimed at the overseas segment, or real UK/EU traffic
# on /care-from-abroad.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=
